[[https://firmware-selector.openwrt.org/?version=SNAPSHOT&target=rockchip%2Farmv8&id=friendlyarm_nanopi-r5s|Download]] an image, decompress, then [[https://github.com/balena-io/etcher|write]] it to a microSD using your PC. Insert the SD into the R5S, plug in power, and it'll boot OpenWrt. You may continue to run it from the SD or copy to the eMMC using ''dd''.

Remember snapshots do not come with LuCI preinstalled, for that you can SSH root@192.168.1.1 and ''opkg update && opkg install luci''.

The root size for snapshots currently does not use all available storage by default. To expand the filesystem see [[:docs:guide-user:advanced:expand_root]] automated script or a [[https://github.com/anaelorlinski/OpenWrt-NanoPi-R2S-R4S-Builds/blob/main/docs/resize-f2fs.md|github guide]].

===== Upgrading =====

To upgrade simply flash a new sysupgrade image. Alternatively users may install ''luci-app-attendedsysupgrade'' for an assisted way to update along with all packages in LuCI.

==== LuCI Upgrade ====

  * Browse to LuCI page: System -> Backup / Flash Firmware
  * Upload image file for sysupgrade
  * Wait for reboot

==== Terminal Upgrade ====

If you are not using LuCI you can SSH: root@192.168.1.1, and use sysupgrade:

<code>
cd /tmp
wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/targets/rockchip/armv8/...[image-filename]
sysupgrade /tmp/[image-filename]
</code>

